00:00:01,470 --> 00:00:02,270
Section twelve.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:04,580
Loop engineering.

3
00:00:06,090 --> 00:00:08,890
Its purpose is to control transitions around inference.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:12,840
We need to know when to run, when to

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:15,520
skip, and when a result has become unsafe to

6
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:15,820
apply.

7
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:19,250
This is application control,

8
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:22,450
not an autonomous model thought-and-action loop.

9
00:00:31,913 --> 00:00:34,973
Preview and worker check admission before constructing the

10
00:00:34,973 --> 00:00:37,033
provider or making a count request.

11
00:00:38,522 --> 00:00:42,442
Transactions claim running attempts so concurrent starts do not

12
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:44,542
independently process the same operation.

13
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:49,270
Previously attempted or uncertain work requires deliberate review,

14
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:50,890
not a silent retry.

15
00:00:52,439 --> 00:00:56,139
Explicit re-analysis can bypass memoization while retaining

16
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:56,779
privacy,

17
00:00:57,579 --> 00:00:58,959
schema, and spending checks.

18
00:01:00,327 --> 00:01:04,147
Classification cohorts use new-analysis, Project, and recency

19
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:06,067
ordering, not a learned ranker.

20
00:01:11,142 --> 00:01:15,222
Automatic organization accumulates eligible changes.

21
00:01:16,722 --> 00:01:20,262
Defaults combine weight six and three distinct entities,

22
00:01:20,922 --> 00:01:22,262
or two new Projects,

23
00:01:23,322 --> 00:01:26,582
followed by a ninety-second quiet period and a thirty-minute

24
00:01:26,582 --> 00:01:28,302
cooldown.

25
00:01:28,302 --> 00:01:30,182
Types and thresholds are configurable.

26
00:01:31,482 --> 00:01:34,302
Consumed event sequences prevent endless rescheduling.

27
00:01:35,522 --> 00:01:37,842
Existing analysis still reconciles locally.

28
00:01:38,622 --> 00:01:42,002
A change upstream cannot be noticed before its content

29
00:01:42,002 --> 00:01:42,682
is fetched.

30
00:01:48,473 --> 00:01:52,713
Revision, generation, policy, and epoch fences bind a response

31
00:01:52,713 --> 00:01:53,633
to current state.

32
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:57,873
If the user edits or resets during generation,

33
00:01:58,773 --> 00:02:03,053
unsafe associations are discarded while historical cost and

34
00:02:03,053 --> 00:02:03,893
processing evidence remain.

35
00:02:05,093 --> 00:02:06,373
Reset uses a scoped,

36
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:10,593
expiring, one-use preview and exact confirmation.

37
00:02:11,393 --> 00:02:14,753
It preserves cost history and readiness reports.

38
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:19,673
These are tested local safeguards, not distributed exactly-once

39
00:02:19,673 --> 00:02:21,873
